{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (per-verb parser and handler edits; the description carries the decisions). Line numbers are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\n`exists`: delete `build_exists` (`_parsers/core/lookups.py:24-28`) and `exists_cli` (`_engine_support/lookups.py:78-91`).\n\n`format` folded into `resolve --display[=MODE]`: `build_resolve` gains `--display` with an optional value; delete `build_format` at `lookups.py:38-43`; `resolve_cli(argv, tracker, repo_root)` pops `--display[=MODE]`, resolves first, then renders via `_render_display()` extracted from `format_cli:117-141`; the `resolve` route adapter flips from `argv_tracker` to `argv_tracker_root` (`_registry.py:223-238`).\n\n`check`: new `build_check` in `_parsers/core/gates.py` with mutually exclusive `--ac/--clarity/--dispatch`, `--output {text,json}`, `--stdin`, `--config PATH`, optional `ticket_id`, deleting `build_check_ac/quality_check/clarity_check` (`gates.py:26-62`); new `check_cli(argv, tracker, repo_root)` in `_engine_support/gates.py` pops the mode flag (more than one gives exit 2) and delegates to the UNCHANGED `check_ac_cli:82`, `clarity_check_cli:211`, `quality_check_cli:388` (JSON via the same `*_compute`, byte-identical); default is dispatch readiness because it is the superset gate (`gates.py:370-385`), while `--ac` survives as a mode because `quality-check` does not strictly subsume `check-ac` (`_count_ac_exit:284` vs `_count_ac_reset:48`); `prog=` at `:90,:241,:396` and usage strings at `:92,:398` become `rebar check ...`.\n\n`tag`/`untag`: delete `build_tag/untag` (`_parsers/core/writes.py:172-185`), `_REGISTRY[\"tag\"/\"untag\"]` (`_commands/__init__.py:62-75`) and the dead confirm branches (`_commands/_confirm.py:138-161`); `edit --add-tag/--remove-tag` already exist (`writes.py:163`, `composer_edit.py:220,391`; both paths emit `TAG_DELTA`, `leaf.py:96-106`); library `rebar.tag/untag` (`_lib_mutations.py:227-252`) untouched; `scripts/retarget_jira_project.py:145` `[\"rebar\",\"untag\",id,tag]` becomes `[\"rebar\",\"edit\",id,f\"--remove-tag={tag}\"]` (plus prose at `:59,:89,:141`).\n\n`show --field NAME`: `build_show` (`_parsers/core/reads.py:32-44`) gains `--field`; delete `_parsers/core/field_reads.py` and `file_impact_cli/verify_commands_cli` (`_engine_support/field_reads.py:55-101`; keep the two library helpers `:36-51`); `_cmd_show` (`reads_cli.py:119`) accepts `--field=`/`--field ` (coalesce), prints `js_safe_dumps(state.get(field), ensure_ascii=False)` one line per id, rejects with `--output llm` (exit 2); extract the render block `:186-207` into `_render_show_state()` first (the function is unbaselined and must stay at or under 15).\n\n`deps --descendants`: `build_deps` (`reads.py:89-96`) gains the flag; delete `_parsers/core/descendants.py`; `_cmd_deps` (`reads_cli.py:397-420`) option guard `:399` admits it and when set prints `list_descendants(root, tracker)` for `root = resolve_ticket_id(id) or id` (same dumps, identical bytes; `--include-archived` ignored and documented); delete `list_descendants_cli` (`descendants.py:76-88`).\n\n`session-logs`: `build_list` (`reads.py:47-75`) gains `--limit N`; delete `build_session_logs` (`:130-137`); `_cmd_list` adds `--limit=` to `_list_known_prefix:245` and `_LIST_VALUE_OPTS`, validation and slice in a helper; first extract the `--priority` block `:305-321` into `_validate_priority()` because `_cmd_list` is at its baseline ceiling of 18 (`.github/complexity-baseline.json` entry `reads_cli.py::_cmd_list 18`); delete `_cmd_session_logs` (`reads_cli.py:356-394`) and `_COMMANDS[\"session-logs\"]:586`; `recent_session_logs_state` (`reads.py:616`) stays for MCP (`list --type` already un-hides session logs, `reads.py:507`; `--sort=-created` exists). The rejected alternative `session-log list` would reject the documented `--output llm` because `session-log` is `confirmable` with `_ALLOWED=(\"text\",\"json\")` (`_commands/_confirm.py:40,84`).\n\nUsage census (docs / root md / guides / templates / skills / CI-scripts / src / tests): exists 3/0/0/0/1/3/2/4; format 1/0/0/0/0/0/1/5; check-ac 2/0/1/2/0/3/2/8; clarity-check 2/0/1/2/0/1/3/6; quality-check 2/0/0/2/0/2/2/4; tag 5/0/0/0/0/2/2/34; untag 2/0/0/0/0/5/2/9; get-file-impact 1/0/0/0/1/1/4/3; get-verify-commands 1/0/0/0/2/1/3/3; list-descendants 1/0/0/0/2/1/4/3; session-logs 6/0/0/2/0/0/2/6. The skill hits are `examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md:88,116,118,119,124,134,388`; the guide hit is `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md:27`; the template hits are `templates/AGENTS.md:71,75` and `templates/rebar-usage.md:47,51`; these are the documentation story's edits.\n\nBaseline maintenance: deleted routes and parsers remove no censused mechanism (`ci_gate`/`env_var`/`config_key` are untouched), so no `--update-stale` is expected; if `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` reports stale rows, run `--update-stale` (operator-sanctioned on the epic) and commit the baseline."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788806006463349335,"uuid":"cee784b0-bbf2-4cd0-86b9-158b475dff5c"}